# JetBrains project files
.idea/

# Browser-automation artifacts
.playwright-mcp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase: everything under supabase/ is PRIVATE unless listed below.
#
# The data files carry rows marked visibility='private' (interview companies,
# unverified claims, private_note text) and the names, employers and profile
# links of people whose consent flag is still false. The whole point of the
# visibility and consent model is that this data never reaches a public repo,
# and these files are the one place it exists in plain text.
#
# They are one-time bootstrap files: run them in the Supabase SQL editor and
# let the database be their home after that.
#
# This is deny-by-default on purpose. Naming each new data file was a rule that
# only held while someone remembered it, and a forgotten line publishes names.
# A new file here is ignored until it is added to the allowlist by hand, which
# is the safe direction to fail in.
#
# To publish a file, add a `!` line. To publish a subdirectory, git must be
# able to descend into it, so unignore the directory before its contents:
#     !supabase/migrations/
#     supabase/migrations/*
#     !supabase/migrations/*-public.sql
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
supabase/*
!supabase/01-schema.sql
!supabase/SETUP.md
